const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 14 Walkthrough: Exchange Office";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 14 walkthrough for the Exchange Office: the hidden calculator's five rates, the six-wheel rate board, the laptop password 6795 and the six-button symbol keypad that finally opens the door.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What are the exchange rates in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 14?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Bolivia 7.67, Argentina 66.47, Azerbaijan 1.89, Canada 1.46 and Costa Rica 629.06. You do not find them written anywhere in the lobby. Tap the LED screen on the blue wall beside the counter, the cover slides aside and a calculator appears with a row of flag buttons: tap a flag and the red display shows that country's rate. Then set the same five values on the big rate board, one row per country."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I open the rate board in the Exchange Office?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The board is behind a metal roll-down shutter above the service counter. The handle that raises it comes from the two-button panel on the wall beside the grey exit door. Once the shutter is up you get five rows, one per country, each with six digit wheels and a pair of up and down triangles per digit."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the laptop password in Chapter 2 Level 14?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "6795. The framed poster in the office shows four geometric shapes in a row; count the sides of each one and enter the counts in the same order. In our playthrough the four shapes gave 6, 7, 9 and 5, which is the password the laptop accepts. The keypad on screen shows the digits as you type, so you can check them before you confirm."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I open the shape cabinet in the office?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The blue octagonal panel on the left-hand cabinets holds the digits 0 to 5, each sitting inside a different shape. Examine the Pattern item in your inventory, then tap the digits from the highest to the lowest: 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0. The cabinet releases the last puzzle piece."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I solve the rope and flag panel?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Once the puzzle pieces are in place the red wall panel becomes a picture of ropes on a blue background: five digit displays along the top, five flags along the bottom. Follow each rope from a flag to the display it ends at and write the number of horizontal stripes that flag has. The ATM in the lobby is the built-in tutorial: it shows a flag and the number 3. The flags are randomised per player, so read your own panel rather than copying a screenshot."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where do I get the handles in the Exchange Office?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "There are two. The first comes from the two-button panel on the wall beside the grey door in the lobby, and it raises the shutter over the rate board. The second is made in the inventory by combining the scissors with the glove, both taken from the first-aid box, and it opens the red safe in the office."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the thermometer showing 37 for?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "We could not find a lock in the Exchange Office that asks for a temperature. The digital thermometer in the first-aid box clearly reads 37, and it is worth looking at, but in our full playthrough nothing consumed it. Treat it as scene dressing unless a later door asks you for a temperature."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does Chapter 2 Level 14 take and what does it pay?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The recording finishes the Exchange Office in 11:56 of level time and pays +50 coins. It is one of the longer rooms in Chapter 2 because it has three areas, the lobby, the office behind it and the exit back in the lobby, and the middle area hides four separate item chains."}}]};
